{{also|kowhai}}
==Maori==

===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|haw|'ōhai||{{taxlink|Sesbania tomentosa|species}}}}, {{cog|ty|ofai||{{taxfmt|Sesbania grandiflora|species}}}} and {{cog|mqm|kohai||{{taxfmt|Caesalpinia pulcherrima|species}}}} from {{inh|mi|poz-pol-pro|*kōfai}}.<ref>{{cite-web|title=Kōfai|work=Te Māra Reo: The Language Garden|year=2022|publisher=Benton Family Trust|url=https://www.temarareo.org/PPN-Kofai.html}}</ref>

Sense of colour from its flower petals, displaced {{m|mi|whero}} entirely (now meaning “red”) and {{m|mi|renga}} partially.<ref name=C>{{cite-journal |last1=Dodgson |first1=Neil |last2=Chen |first2=Victoria |last3=Zahido |first3=Meimuna |date=Nov 2024 |title=The colonisation of the colour pink: variation and change in Māori’s colour lexicon |journal=Linguistics |pages=14-15, 23-4 |doi=10.1515/ling-2023-0059}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|mi|/kɔːɸai/}}

===Noun===
{{mi-noun}}

# Any of several small woody [[legume]] trees in the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Sophora|genus}} native to New Zealand that have yellow flowers. The national flower of New Zealand.
# [[yellow]]
#: {{syn|mi|renga}}

